# Local package import shadowing repair

Classification: engineering audit and regression repair. No mathematical promotion.

The independent review of PR1003 at
`d54097cb96b1c5fcbb6eca57843b53e7b8a6dd2e` found that the import audit considered
`math.py` but omitted `math/__init__.py` when deciding whether the standard
library's `math` was shadowed. A package could omit that local initializer from
its input list. The isolated filesystem would then supply standard-library
behavior even though the full repository had a different local implementation.

The reproduced counterexample has `math.sqrt` return `99` locally, while the
declared script asserts `math.sqrt(4)==2`. A package-README-only change was
classified as targeted replay and passed using the isolated standard library.
This did not set `full_verified`, but silently changed import resolution and
failed the declared-input contract.

The repair checks both module files and regular-package initializers in the
repository and entry-script search roots. An undeclared local candidate requires
review. A declared initializer is materialized and replayed with its actual
behavior. Two executable regressions cover both outcomes, including refusing
the original undeclared case before replay. The existing conservative handling
of other Python capabilities remains explicit in the protocol.

## Exact verification evidence

The repair was first committed as
`6d1171fee7359c62f9d6f8fa8a5d89983088b1df`, directly above the reviewed PR head.
The locked Python 3.14.7 environment passed 77 focused checks, then all 14 full
verification stages: 195 tooling tests, 18 repository tests, 65 research tests,
and all 94 registered certificates. The full run took 467.121 seconds with
`origin/main` pinned to `5dcbdc3dfa1f9be370602cc54d50e68eabb88f56`.

During that verification, PR1003 was merged independently at
`aa9b45669ce7200a99f6ec4c58e1e3c23a57387f`. The identical four-file repair was
therefore replayed onto that integrated base for a separate maintenance PR.
The full log certifies its named tested head; final integrated-source and
private-export verification remain separate closeout requirements.

Both hosted rollout variables were freshly observed absent through the
repository API. This repair changes neither workflow activation nor repository
settings. Local scoped replay and complete repository verification remain
distinct results, and neither constitutes independent human mathematical review.
